From: Florian Fuchs <fuchsfl@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] sh: maple: Put the bus timeout into bits 31:16

The maple speed register (SB_MSYS) holds the response time-out counter
in bits 31:16, in units of 20 ns, as used by KallistiOS
(MAPLE_SPEED_TIMEOUT(n) = n << 16, programmed with 50000, i.e. 1 ms).
MAPLE_TIMEOUT() shifted by 15 instead, so MAPLE_TIMEOUT(0xFFFF) set a
time-out of 0x7FFF, about 0.65 ms, plus a stray bit 15.

On a real VMU the reply to an LCD block write arrives later than that:
the frame is drawn, but the maple core sees MAPLE_RESPONSE_NONE, treats
it as a possible hot unplug, marks the device busy == 2 and the LCD
driver returns -ENXIO for every frame. Because the memory card shares
the device's busy flag, a concurrent flash write then fails with -ENXIO
too ("VMU write failing with error -6", lost async page write).

Shift by 16, and program the 50000 of KallistiOS instead of 0xFFFF: with
0xFFFF in bits 31:16 the maple DMA of a real Dreamcast never times out.
As soon as a device does not answer, e.g. a VMU that was just pulled or
a port that gets a device plugged in mid-transfer, SB_MDST stays busy
forever, no DMA end interrupt arrives and the whole bus stops: no more
hotplug detection, controller, keyboard or mouse input.

---
diff --git a/arch/sh/include/mach-dreamcast/mach/maple.h b/arch/sh/include/mach-dreamcast/mach/maple.h
--- a/arch/sh/include/mach-dreamcast/mach/maple.h
+++ b/arch/sh/include/mach-dreamcast/mach/maple.h
@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@
 
 #define MAPLE_MAGIC    0x6155404f
 #define MAPLE_2MBPS    0
-#define MAPLE_TIMEOUT(n) ((n)<<15)
+#define MAPLE_TIMEOUT(n) ((n)<<16)
 
 /* Function codes */
 #define MAPLE_FUNC_CONTROLLER 0x001
diff --git a/drivers/sh/maple/maple.c b/drivers/sh/maple/maple.c
--- a/drivers/sh/maple/maple.c
+++ b/drivers/sh/maple/maple.c
@@ -103,13 +103,16 @@
 	__raw_writel(1, MAPLE_TRIGTYPE);
 	/*
 	* Maple system register
-	* bits 31 - 16	timeout in units of 20nsec
+	* bits 31 - 16	timeout in units of 20nsec; use the 50000 (1 ms) of
+	*		KallistiOS: with 0xFFFF the DMA never times out on
+	*		real hardware and the bus hangs once a device does
+	*		not answer (unplugged VMU, port plugged mid-transfer)
 	* bit 12	hard trigger - set 0 to keep responding to VBLANK
 	* bits 9 - 8	set 00 for 2 Mbps, 01 for 1 Mbps
 	* bits 3 - 0	delay (in 1.3ms) between VBLANK and start of DMA
 	* max delay is 11
 	*/
-	__raw_writel(MAPLE_2MBPS | MAPLE_TIMEOUT(0xFFFF), MAPLE_SPEED);
+	__raw_writel(MAPLE_2MBPS | MAPLE_TIMEOUT(50000), MAPLE_SPEED);
 	__raw_writel(virt_to_phys(maple_sendbuf), MAPLE_DMAADDR);
 	__raw_writel(1, MAPLE_ENABLE);
 }
-- 
